12611	1Li3gtZrk3g	55385	Arsène Lupin, the Collection: Netflix Series Special Edition - 3 Books In 1	This first volume of the Arsène Lupin Collection includes three of the greatest masterpieces from the series that inspired the Netflix show. 1. The Crystal Stopper Once more Lupin is at large, always one step ahead of the law. But this time he may have met his match in Deputy Alexis Daubrecq. This book was inspired by the Panama Canal Scandal, the largest monetary corruption scandal of the 19th century. In a gripping story centered around theft, deception, murder, and blackmail, the ingenious criminal manages to stay several steps ahead of the authorities, until a thrilling final showdown has terrible consequences for one of the characters. Can the world's greatest thief get his act together, save his arrested men from the guillotine, and recover his lost honor? 2. The Hollow Needle (for which Maurice Leblanc was awarded the French Legion of Honour for literature) The first detective on the case is Isidore Beautrelet, a precocious teenager who wears a fake beard to disguise the fact that he has not yet graduated from high school. Lupin is chasing the most valuable object he has ever had the opportunity to steal: the Hollow Needle. In the Arsène Lupin universe, the Hollow Needle is the second secret of Marie Antoinette and Alessandro Cagliostro, the hidden fortune of the kings of France. Passed down by the kings of France since the time of Julius Caesar, it holds a secret that could undo the republic. The unexpected twists and turns of the tale reach a crescendo when Beautrelet arrives at Étretat and discovers a secret passageway within a rock formation built into the cliffs. Visitors today can easily identify this exact spot on the coastline, a 'needle' shaped like an elephant's trunk dipped into the sea. Here Beautrelet stumbled upon a veritable Aladdin's Cave, with original paintings by Botticelli, Leonardo da Vinci and Rembrandt lining the walls. "These are the original pictures, patiently collected in all the museums of Europe," Lupin gloated, "where I have replaced them, like an honest man, with first-rate copies!". 3. The Golden Triangle (also known as The Return of Arsène Lupin) As our tale opens, Arsene Lupin is but a memory. We see his picturesque grave, and perhaps we take a moment to mourn his passing. But soon a mystery comes into focus. It tells the story of a war veteran Captain Patrice Belval who stops a kidnapping attempt on a young nurse. As layer upon layer of conspiracy emerges with no obvious thread to follow, there's only one man who can be counted on to uncover the truth.	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/1Li3gtZrk3g/hqdefault.jpg	2025-05-18 13:35:39.926286+00	1410
